Z||000000||fiero mistress||05-24-2000||11:10 AM||||Hi everyone!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I have been reading the forum for a little while, but now I am joining the conversations!<P>I have a red, stock, 84SE.  It has good interior and runs great, but needs a paint job.  Working on it slowly.<P>What I really want is a V6 Fiero like my husbands (Gold86SE).  I enjoy driving mine, but it is a little too slow!<P>FieroSTETZ has one almost exactly like my husband's (matching Fieros?!), but it needs a clutch cylinder.  I don't know how hard it is to replace, I am sure we could handle it.<P>My main problem is getting it from CA to TX.  Or should I just give up on this one?<BR>I would apreciate any suggestions!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>Here is the link to FieroSTETZ's sale page <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/000804.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/000804.html</A> <P>Thanks!<BR>Mistress||||reg||7
Z||000001||lennyb4||05-24-2000||11:33 AM||||Well first off welcome to the forum  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> . I would say it sounds like a good buy, BUT i would want to actually see it (or atleast pics) prior to agreeing on anything. As for transporting it, i havent a clue. If its not too far maybe rent a car trailer and drive down on a weekend to get it. This way you could also handle the title change there.||||reg||6
Z||000002||fiero mistress||05-24-2000||11:37 AM||||Some good points!  It's a little over 1,300 miles from me.<P>Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Flash Box||05-24-2000||11:45 AM||||Welcome Fiero Mistress!! I also have a 84 SE except mine is black. My Brother-In-Law just moved from MD to TX. What is going on down there you are like the 5th person I know that is moving to TX!!<p>[This message has been edited by Flash Box (edited 05-24-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000004||phillip||05-24-2000||11:50 AM||||i've changed my clutch cyl. if you knew me that would be proof of how easy it is.<P>i rented a u-haul truck and tow dolly a couple of weeks ago to pick up my fiero. worked out well, but i only had to go 165 mls. though.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fiero mistress||05-24-2000||12:00 PM||||Well, Flash Box, I have lived in TX since 1st grade and I love it here!  You have to visit to understand.  Come on down and visit the ALAMO!  We have a great Fiero club called the "Alamo Area Fiero Owners" (AAFO).<P>The 86SE I want to purchase is in CA, 1,300 miles from me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> and I am trying to figure out how to purchase it and get it to Texas, or to just give up on it...I really want a V6 though...<P>phillip, I will check on the price of renting a uhaul, but it is a good 2-3 day drive one-way.  I am going to start looking locally, but I doubt I will find one for this price.<P>Thanks for the welcome!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Mistress||||reg||1
Z||000006||lawrence||05-24-2000||12:48 PM||||I live near Cleveland and bought my car in Chicago (about 350 mi?).  I bought a one-way plane ticket for $79 and drove it back.  I flew out in the morning and pulled into the garage at 7 PM.<P>Good luck,<P>-L<BR> <A HREF="http://members.nccw.net/webe" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nccw.net/webe</A>  - WebElectric Magazine||||reg||1
Z||000007||fiero mistress||05-24-2000||01:10 PM||||lawrence, I wish it was that easy.  The best price for having it delivered that I could find was $550, and we can't take a week off to go get it.<P>I guess I will just look for one around here (San Antonio).  Not to mention I could put the money into the other two we are driving now.  My need for speed will have to wait.<P>Thanks, all!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Mistress||||reg||9
Z||000008||Oreif||05-24-2000||01:12 PM||||Welcome to the Forum! As for transporting the car, There are company's that will pick up the car and deliver it to your door but they are costly. I looked into getting a non-driveable GT from California and have it delivered to Chicago, The price was $725.00 to ship it and another $150 for towing because it wasn't driveable. If you wanted to do it that way it would porbably be cheaper for you (less miles) but still up there. Depending on the cost of the car and how bad you want it,  the question would be is the shipping cost worth it?||||reg||1
Z||000009||olympic||05-24-2000||04:35 PM||||Welcome...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/nsmailJA.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000010||stimpy||05-24-2000||07:30 PM||||Olympic, you slay me! Too much fun lol.  <BR>As far as transporting cars, I had my non running Fiero transported from Tracy CA (central valley) to Okla City for $300! The key is t tell the guy giving the quote that you aren't picky about when it comes, and to just pick it up when they have an open space on a truck going through the area.  I will look for the name & # of the co. which hauled my car. If it is drivable, then you should be able to make it in a weekend if you don't mind spending MANY hours in a fiero. I drove my other car the same route (tracy to okc) in 20 hours over 2.5 days.  ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Coconut||05-24-2000||09:10 PM||||Hello fiero mistress, Welcome to the Forum! I know you'll enjoy it here. If it turns out that you decide to get the V6, I would go with the suggestion of the tow trailer. If it turns out you don't, be patient.... the opportunity WILL arise. Just a matter of being at the right place at the right time! Kinda like how I met Mrs.Coconut!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Keep on Cruisin'  Coconut||||reg||7
Z||000012||fiero mistress||05-24-2000||11:02 PM||||Thanks everyone for the advice and welcome!<P>I just found out there is a Gold 86SE VERY near me for $700.  It just won't start (starter?), needs a paint job (so does my 84), and a little work on the tie-rods (we have spares).  The owner has been bitted with Mustang fever (whatever THAT is!!) and he is just wanting to GET RID OF IT!<P>Just what I am looking for, a fixer-upper.  The only kind of Fiero I can afford at this time.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I am soooo excited, I can't wait for him to return our call.  Maybe we will have matching Fieros yet...wish me luck!||||reg||7
Z||000013||FieroGTGirl||05-25-2000||02:07 AM||||WELCOME MISTRESS!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>So very nice to see another FEMALE around here... Boy the testosterone level has been TOOOOOOOOO high for me.. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  <P>These guys are GREAT though! I am starting to feel like "part of the family"...LOL <P>I hope you get the Gold SE V6!  Believe me V6 is very fun.  Especially when you get the car fishtailing on ya...(shhh!!Don't tell my hubby I said that) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>BTW~ I have a 86 Black GT and trust me you will love upgrading from the 4 cyl to the 6 cyl.  <P>GOOD LUCK!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000014||MikeE||05-25-2000||04:40 AM||||Hello fiero mistress,<BR>I too am a new member, as of today.  However, unlike you, I only discovered this list today while reading a posting about Paul Herder's Quad4 Fiero on the Quad4 list.  Have you considered an engine swap in your existing car as an alternative.  Having both driven a 2m4 and owned an 87 2m6 SE, I didn't find the V6 to be significantly faster than the 4 and it's definately lacking in high RPM power.  Swapping in one of the larger V6s from the 2.8-3.4 60 degree pushrod series would yield more power and should be fairly simple since the correct motor mounts already exist.  If a suitable wrecked donor car could be found, it could probably be done for the same cost as buying a V6 Fiero but the result would be more of a personal statement. Something like the 3800, 3.4 DOHC, or northstar would be preferable but quite a bit more expensive.  This is just my two cents since one of the plusses that originally lead me to the Fiero was the vast multitude of engine swap possibilities.||||reg||6
Z||000015||fiero mistress||05-25-2000||04:12 PM||||Hi, MikeE and FieroGTGirl!<P>I might consider a conversion in the future, but for now I will just have to settle for borrowing my husband's 86SE when I want to romp on it.  With his I got my first kill a couple of weeks ago!  Some girl in a late model ricer.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero mistress (edited 05-25-2000).]||||reg||1
